  "_doc": "A fleet battle as the campaign has it, to watch from the bridge and to measure the war's scale with reinforcements: the Aquila held at rest 16 km behind the 7th Fleet's line (two Praetorians with their hangar decks, destroyer wings on both flanks), the Kharon Mandate's Interdiction Fleet coming at her from the east (three Acheron carriers with their screen, a Styx line, two raider wedges). Thirty-seven ships and a hundred-odd craft at the start; five waves keep the battle fed (Mandate raiders at 90 s, an ASTRA relief column at 170 s, a second Mandate carrier group at 200 s, a Styx strike line at 330 s, an ASTRA destroyer flotilla at 380 s, a third Mandate carrier group at 460 s, a second ASTRA relief column at 560 s). The class table has no ASTRA carrier but the Aquila herself, so her own air group launches from her bow tubes and the Praetorians host wings (a bench licence). astra.war.scenario fleet_battle (the Aquila is in it: the file says so); hold|speed=N|heading=D after it move her. tools/war.py run --scenario fleet_battle --seconds 900 reads the cost per tick.",
